NEXT TEST: Test 1, run 7: DM + player script, first-time consent, player stops
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why
  Run 6 gave the first scored baseline with the DM alone. Still open: a scored run
  with two speakers, the first-time consent question, and a player stopping.

Where it runs
  Cloud test server, Docker Compose (postgres, core, ears), development branch,
  TRANSCRIBER=whisper-local small, DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1. Server session watches logs.

Before the test (owner)
  [ ] Tell the server session how many people (1 = DM only, 2 = DM + player, ...)
      and send the matching script from docs/test-scripts/ (paste it into Discord)
  [ ] Someone who has NOT agreed yet (ideally a third account) in voice before
      /dmbot start; or the player presses Stop recording me during this run and the
      first-time question is checked next session
  [ ] At each (( dramatic pause )): mute, count to three, unmute
  [ ] Note: packet loss tool on/off, each reader's Discord noise suppression

What to check
  - Private message to everyone in voice; the new one gets "Can DMbot record
    you...?"; the phone preview reads well
  - I consent -> capture within seconds; Stop recording me -> gone from the next check
  - Wait for the script's last line in a capture check before /dmbot stop
  - Whisper keeps up (the stall fix #137 is live since 22:33): a slow clip shows as a
    warning, not a freeze
  - Score it (docs/test-scripts/README.md): audio from ears lines, pieces of speech,
    Part 1 of 35 (dm-and-player) or 33 (dm-only), Part 2 of 12, whisper, first word
    after each split pause (#121)
  - Compare with run 6 (local Whisper small): Part 1 33/33, Part 2 7/12, whisper all

